    "#h-sc + p": "Switch shocks on, set their size, and see the price and your cost move. PET has no published stocks, so the model links price to slack relative to output (labelled stocks-to-use below). Slack starts as idle capacity. Restarts or weak demand add to it, because they add supply buyers must absorb; cuts or strong demand take from it. The elasticity is an assumption you can change.",
